 "api_error_status": null,
 "result": "**Decorator:** `needs_app_scope` in `src/tessel/cli.py:380`. It's this repo's version of Flask's `with_appcontext`. It loads the app if none is active and runs your callback inside `app.app_context()`.\n\n- If you register the command with `app.cli.command()` or `bundle.cli.command()`, you don't need to add it. `AppGroup.command` (`src/tessel/cli.py:405`) wraps callbacks in it by default. Pass `needs_app_scope=False` to turn that off.\n- If you use a plain `@click.command()`, add `@needs_app_scope` yourself.\n\n**Class that loads the app:** `LaunchInfo` in `src/tessel/cli.py:293`. Its `load_app()` method (line 333) returns the app. `pass_script_info` (line 375) injects it into a command if you need it directly.\n\nThe top-level CLI group is `TesselGroup` (line 531). It subclasses `AppGroup` and calls `info.load_app()` (lines 623 and 645) to find the app's registered commands.",
